// The epilogue (bible 7.4, 9; character-bibles.md). A walk through Halden, then one outer region, then Marrow,
// under thirty minutes. The walk's order is Endings.EpilogueWalk: Fixed goes to the quay, Open to Kettil's Rest,
// the Unwritten to the Quiet House; the Rest goes from Halden straight to the Hollow.
// Marrow's verdict is its last original word, or none. The last line is Wren's, in her atlas, by her most-used voice.

title: Epilogue_Pell
---
<<if flag("ending.chosen") == 1>>
    Pell: I sit the exam next spring. I know. It's always next spring. I sit it anyway. #still #face:grave #line:0d26e8b
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 2>>
    Pell: I'm leaving the Plateau. Tomorrow. I've packed five things. Three. One. #face:bright #line:07398e5
    Pell: Which, technically, means I'm ready. #face:bright #line:07c71ba
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 3>>
    Pell: I keep the Hall's ledger by hand now. Every place, every day. Somebody should write down what's still here. #face:grave #line:06b4003
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 4>>
    Isolde: Again. Slower. Let the pen find the line; don't push it. #line:0db7392
    Hall: On the desk, open, an atlas in a journeyman's hand. #line:02681ff
    Pell: She's a good teacher. She keeps looking at the door. #face:grave #line:02632ac
<<else>>
    Pell: Nothing's happened yet. I'd know. I write everything down. #line:0c257e9
<<endif>>
===

title: Epilogue_Sable
---
<<if flag("ending.chosen") == 1>>
    Sable: Prices are the same. #still #face:grave #line:05ccf79
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 2>>
    Sable: Prices went up. Good. Things do. #face:bright #line:059dba5
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 3>>
    Sable: One. Two. Three boats back. I'm counting again. Out loud. Don't tell anyone. #face:grave #line:0323630
<<else>>
    Sable: Boat's in. You're early, or I'm late. Neither's free. #line:08e2d51
<<endif>>
===

title: Epilogue_Runa
---
<<if flag("ending.chosen") == 1>>
    Runa: Forty-two. Forty-two, Wren. Forty-two. #still #face:grave #line:0f4030f
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 2>>
    Runa: Forty-three! That's her, from Merrow's End. I'm teaching her the walk. She's terrible. We'll learn it walking. #line:0536d13
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 3>>
    Runa: Thirty-nine. We were forty-two. Thirty-nine. I keep counting. That's the point. #face:grave #line:056f611
<<else>>
    Runa: Forty-two, Wren. Stand where I can count you. #face:bright #line:0326f55
<<endif>>
===

title: Epilogue_Teodor
---
<<if flag("ending.chosen") == 1>>
    Teodor: Aldermere was. The eleven were. I say it that way now. It is easier, and it is worse. #face:grave #line:0e2e496
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 2>>
    Teodor: The House teaches the thread now. To Guild journeymen. They are terrible at it. They are learning. #face:bright #line:0ba5837
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 3>>
    Teodor: I walk Aldermere's bounds every evening, alone. And it holds, cartographer. It holds. #face:bright #line:08fcbe5
<<else>>
    Teodor: Sit, cartographer. The House is quiet for that reason, and no other. #line:07a40b0
<<endif>>
===

title: Epilogue_Marrow
---
<<if flag("ending.chosen") == 1>>
    Ilse: The same bread. The same sunset. Every evening. #face:grave #line:0792e00
    Hollow: The grey chick is grey no longer. It is bright, and beautiful. #line:05a6967
    Marrow: Same. #echo:ilse #line:05ca432
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 2>>
    Hollow: The Hollow in colour, slowly, grey still at the edges. #line:0d5244b
    Hollow: The chick laughs. #line:0b2f562
    Marrow: Skywalk. #line:093cc21
    <<flag marrow.words 4>>
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 3>>
    Hollow: The chick fades, gently, holding Wren's wing. It is not afraid. #line:0fa6a1c
    Marrow: Look. #line:06d2a44
    <<flag marrow.words 4>>
<<elseif flag("ending.chosen") == 4>>
    Hollow: The Hollow, grey. No chick at the edge of the village. #line:06366e7
<<endif>>
<<if dominant_voice() == "warden">>
    Atlas: In Wren's hand, the last page: everyone I could, carried out. #line:0c5e477
<<elseif dominant_voice() == "drift">>
    Atlas: In Wren's hand, the last page, left blank. On purpose. #line:060b5aa
<<else>>
    Atlas: In Wren's hand, the last page: everything I saw, drawn true. #line:0f4d228
<<endif>>
<<flag epilogue.done 1>>
===
